# agents/

The nine agent profiles — six actors and three `user-*` personas. (This
note lives in .gitkeep because a README.md here would be parsed as a
profile and fail `claude plugin validate --strict`.)

Actors: `flywheel-dispatch`, `flywheel-intent-conductor`,
`flywheel-bolt-conductor`, `flywheel-design-session`,
`flywheel-interactive-session`, `flywheel-construction-session`.
Personas — lenses a review session runs under, never actors:
`user-data-scientist`, `user-devops-engineer`, `user-app-developer`.

**The profiles keep their `flywheel-` prefix where the skills drop theirs, and
the asymmetry is deliberate.** `claude --agent` resolves a plugin agent by its
bare name as well as its namespaced one, so the bare name is the addressable
one and has to stay globally unique. A skill invoked as `/flywheel:inception`
carries its namespace in the invocation; an agent launched as
`--agent flywheel-intent-conductor` does not.
